# A dry snare, one node: a body on 200 Hz that snaps down onto it in 5 ms,
# with its second mode at 319 Hz, under wires in a wide band at 5 kHz, a
# little more wires than body, lightly driven. Measured: the body's loudest
# bin at 200 Hz; 20 dB down at 64 ms, 40 at 122, over (60 dB down) at 170 ms,
# the wires' decay, the body gone by 110; the node peaks at 0.96 of full
# scale. balance= sets wires against body, body= and wires= their lengths.
instrument crack {
  snare(200hz, snap=5ms, body=110ms, wires=170ms, band=5000hz, balance=0.55, drive=0.2) as s
  s > out
}
